course: dictionary
lesson: 10877
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Read the whole sentence, then ask which meaning fits.
explain: «Zara built her school project, a Roman villa, in Minecraft.» The word Roman is the clue. Here villa means a big country house and farm owned by a rich Roman family, as in history lessons about Britain.
explain: «In a lounge in Auckland, Alfie watches young people in a villa shouting at each other.» Here villa means a house of a certain old style in a town, which is how people use the word in the UK, Australia and New Zealand.
explain: «Jamal from Birmingham says he is English, British, Black and a Villa fan.» The capital V and the word fan show that Villa is the name of a football club, not a house. Capital letters can be a clue, but always check the rest of the sentence too.
fact: «Villa» means a large, comfortable house, often with a garden, in the country or by the sea, especially in a warm place.
fact: A Roman villa was a big country house and farm owned by a rich Roman family.
fact: Roman villas often had mosaic floors, central heating and baths, and pupils study them in history lessons.
fact: In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, a villa can also be an old-style house in a town.
fact: A capital V in «Villa» can be the name of a football club, so check the context before you decide.
exercise: «Zara built her school project, a Roman villa, in Minecraft.» In this sentence, what is a villa? | A type of tiny boat | *A big country house and farm owned by a rich Roman family | A small shop in a town | A football club
exercise: Jamal says he is a «Villa fan». Why does Villa have a capital V? | It is at the start of a sentence | *It is the name of a football club | It means the same as a villa with a pool | It is a house by the sea
exercise: «In a lounge in Auckland, Alfie watches young people in a villa shouting at each other.» Which meaning fits here? | *A house of a certain old style in a town | A holiday house with a pool, far from any town | A rich Roman country farm | A tall tower
test: Which sentence uses villa to mean a large, comfortable house with a garden in a warm place? | Jamal is a Villa fan | Zara built a Roman villa in Minecraft | *Families may rent a villa with a pool on holiday | Alfie watches young people in a villa in Auckland
test: Which clue tells you that «a Roman villa» is about history? | The word fan | *The word Roman, which points to ancient history | The word lounge | The word Minecraft
exam: What does villa mean in «a Roman villa», and which clue helps you? | *A rich Roman family's big country house and farm, because the word Roman points to history | A football club, because of the capital letter | A house in a town, because of the word Minecraft | A small wooden house, because of the word school
